# Locked SEO Template Rules

This site is a **reusable game-cheat template**. SEO structure is locked. When retargeting another game (e.g. Fortnite, Apex), keep the same system — only swap brand/game tokens.

## Language (locked)

- Use **simple, short English**. One idea per sentence.
- Prefer plain words: buy, setup, status, features, store — not jargon walls.
- No keyword stuffing. Primary keyword appears naturally in title, H1, intro, and once in body.
- Avoid long dashes of SEO filler (“also searched as…”, map laundry lists) unless the page truly needs it.

## Page formula (locked)

Every product page must follow:

1. **Title** (~50–60 chars): `{Game} {Topic} | {Brand}` — use `seoTitle()` from `src/data/brand.ts`
2. **Meta description** (~140–160 chars): benefit + what’s included + platform — use `seoDescription()` / tokens
3. **H1**: short label matching nav when possible (`Features`, `Store`, `Status`, `Preview`)
4. **Intro**: 1–2 short sentences
5. **Sections**: 2–4 max; each has one H2, one short paragraph, optional bullet list
6. **CTA**: Buy now + one secondary link

## Nav / IA labels (locked meaning)

| Nav label | Purpose | Do not rename meaning |
|-----------|---------|------------------------|
| Preview | What the product is (EN nav: **Hacks** → `/pubg-cheats/`) | Not a blog |
| Features | What’s included | Not pricing |
| Store | Plans / buy (EN nav: **Store** → `/pubg-cheat-price/`) | Not feature list |
| Status | Patch maintenance updates (EN nav: **Updates**) | Not “undetected” claims |
| Reviews | Social proof (`/pubg-cheat-reviews/`) | Keep real reviews |

## Tokens to swap for a new game

**Single source of truth:** `src/data/brand.ts` (or Brand Studio at `/brand-studio/` during `astro dev`)

Then run `npm run sync:brand` (also runs on `prebuild`). Brand Studio does this automatically on Save.

Also update as needed:

- FAQs / reviews meta in `src/data/site.ts` (keep `{brand}` `{game}` `{antiCheat}` `{email}` tokens)
- EN copy in `src/data/i18n/simple-pages.ts` and keyword hubs in `src/data/pubg-keyword-pages.ts`
- Owner keywords: `src/data/pubg-keyword-registry.ts` (one term → one URL; no stuffing)
- Images: `src/data/product-images.ts`, `public/images/pubg-screenshot-*.webp`, hero `public/videos/PUBG_Cinematic_5s_removed_1080p60.webp`
- Sitemap labels in `brand.sitemap` — domain is always `brand.url`; run `npm run sync:brand` before build
- Site colors in `brand.theme` — PUBG canvas: `#0D0A14` main, `#0F0C18` panel, `#0E0B17` hover, `#0F0C19` elevated, `#040306` edge/shadow
- Canonical keyword URLs (EN): `/`, `/pubg-cheats/`, `/pubg-cheat-price/`, `/best-pubg-cheats/`, `/pubg-cheat-reviews/`, `/pubg-aimbot/`, `/pubg-esp/`
- Anti-cheat copy must use **BattlEye** (`{antiCheat}`), not VAC or other games
- Purchase CTAs → `brand.checkoutUrl` with `rel="sponsored nofollow"` (no affiliate disclosure page)

Do **not** hardcode brand/domain in components — use `siteConfig`, `productInfo`, `blogLabel`, or `fillBrandTokens()`.

Do **not** invent a new SEO architecture, title pattern, or dense paragraph style.

## Schema / technical (locked)

- Keep FAQPage, Product / AggregateRating, BreadcrumbList patterns.
- One canonical URL per page; trailing slash convention unchanged.
- Homepage FAQ uses short answers; each question can have its own URL.
- Sitemaps stay generated the same way.
- `brand.url` must match Astro `site`, robots.txt Sitemap, and webmanifest (via sync-brand).

## Bad vs good

```text
❌ BAD H1: Ultimate Undetected Valorant Cheats Feature Control List 2026
✅ GOOD H1: Features

❌ BAD intro: Valorant Cheats is the undetected valorant cheats package also searched as valorant cheats…
✅ GOOD intro: Everything included in one license for Valorant on Windows PC.

❌ BAD: Hardcode "Valorant Cheats" in Hero.astro
✅ GOOD: {siteConfig.name}
```
